o be used to follow batch growth of Streptomyces. Improvements in both biomass yield and product yield of the pigmented antibiotic actinorhodin were found to result from the incorporation of Junlon into minimal medium.\nL42: This is a preview of subscription content, to check access.\nL43: ## Access this article\nL44: \nL45: Log in via an institution\nL46: \nL47: ## Subscribe and save\nL48: \nL49: Springer+\nL50: \nL51: from €37.37 /Month\nL52: \nL53:   * Starting from 10 chapters or articles per month\nL54:   * Access and download chapters and articles from more than 300k books and 2,500 journals\nL55:   * Cancel anytime\nL56: 【19†View plans】\nL57: ## Buy Now\nL58: \nL59: [Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input]\nL60: \nL61: Buy article PDF 39,95 €\nL62: \nL63: Price includes VAT (Denmark)\nL64: \nL65: Instant access to the full article PDF.\nL66: \nL67: 【20†Institutional subscriptions†www.springernature.com】\nL68: \nL69: ### Similar content being viewed by others\nL70: \nL71: 【21†Image†media.springernature.com】\nL72: \nL73: ### 【22†Medium composition and aeration to high (R,R)-2,3-butanediol and acetoin production by Paenibacillus polymyxa in fed-batch mode】\nL74: \nL75: Article 05 April 2023\nL76: \nL77: 【23†Image†media.springernature.com】\nL78: ### 【24†Motility in liquid and semisolid media of Paenibacillus polymyxa associative rhizobacteria differing in exopolysaccharide yield and properties】\nL79: \nL80: Article 06 May 2017\nL81: \nL82: 【25†Image†media.springernature.com】\nL83: \nL84: ### 【26†Synthesis of (poly)gallic acid in a bacterial growth medium】\nL85: \nL86: Article 01 April 2020\nL87: ## References\nL88: \nL89:   * Elmayergi H, Scharer JM, Moo-Young M (1973) Effect of polymer additives on fermentation parameters in a culture of Aspergillus niger. Biotechnol Bioeng 15:845–859\nL90: \nL91:   * Flowers TH, Williams ST (1977) Measurement of growth rates of Streptomycetes: comparison of turbidimetric and gravimetric techniques. J Gen 